    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-49326",
      "knowledge_point_id": "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. We can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{9-9{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-9\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-9(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
