  "canonical_examples": [
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-477",
      "knowledge_point_id": "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-478",
      "knowledge_point_id": "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-479",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    },
    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-480",
      "knowledge_point_id": "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
        "difficulty",
        "answer_fields"
      ]
    }
